{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "DS-0001",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "':latest' tag used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0001\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: ':latest' tag used\nMessage: Specify a tag in the 'FROM' statement for image 'node'\nLink: [DS-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001)\nWhen using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0001**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|MEDIUM|':latest' tag used|Specify a tag in the 'FROM' statement for image 'node'|[DS-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0001)|\n\nWhen using a 'FROM' statement you should use a specific tag to avoid uncontrolled behavior when the image is updated."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0002",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Image user should not be 'root'"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Running containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0002\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Image user should not be 'root'\nMessage: Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user as argument\nLink: [DS-0002](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002)\nRunning containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0002**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|HIGH|Image user should not be 'root'|Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user as argument|[DS-0002](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002)|\n\nRunning containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0005",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ADD instead of COPY"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "You should use COPY instead of ADD unless you want to extract a tar file. Note that an ADD command will extract a tar file, which adds the risk of Zip-based vulnerabilities. Accordingly, it is advised to use a COPY command, which does not extract tar files."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0005",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0005\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: ADD instead of COPY\nMessage: Consider using 'COPY . /app' command instead of 'ADD . /app'\nLink: [DS-0005](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0005)\nYou should use COPY instead of ADD unless you want to extract a tar file. Note that an ADD command will extract a tar file, which adds the risk of Zip-based vulnerabilities. Accordingly, it is advised to use a COPY command, which does not extract tar files.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0005**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|LOW|ADD instead of COPY|Consider using 'COPY . /app' command instead of 'ADD . /app'|[DS-0005](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0005)|\n\nYou should use COPY instead of ADD unless you want to extract a tar file. Note that an ADD command will extract a tar file, which adds the risk of Zip-based vulnerabilities. Accordingly, it is advised to use a COPY command, which does not extract tar files."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0026",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No HEALTHCHECK defined"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "You should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0026\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: No HEALTHCHECK defined\nMessage: Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile\nLink: [DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0026**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|LOW|No HEALTHCHECK defined|Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile|[DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)|\n\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0029",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "'apt-get' missing '--no-install-recommends'"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "'apt-get' install should use '--no-install-recommends' to minimize image size."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0029",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0029\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: 'apt-get' missing '--no-install-recommends'\nMessage: '--no-install-recommends' flag is missed: 'apt-get update \u0026\u0026 apt-get install -y curl'\nLink: [DS-0029](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0029)\n'apt-get' install should use '--no-install-recommends' to minimize image size.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0029**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|HIGH|'apt-get' missing '--no-install-recommends'|'--no-install-recommends' flag is missed: 'apt-get update \u0026\u0026 apt-get install -y curl'|[DS-0029](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0029)|\n\n'apt-get' install should use '--no-install-recommends' to minimize image size."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0001",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Can elevate its own privileges"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0001\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: Can elevate its own privileges\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation' to false\nLink: [KSV-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001)\nA program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0001**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|MEDIUM|Can elevate its own privileges|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation' to false|[KSV-0001](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001)|\n\nA program inside the container can elevate its own privileges and run as root, which might give the program control over the container and node."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0003",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0003\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should add 'ALL' to 'securityContext.capabilities.drop'\nLink: [KSV-0003](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003)\nThe container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0003**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should add 'ALL' to 'securityContext.capabilities.drop'|[KSV-0003](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003)|\n\nThe container should drop all default capabilities and add only those that are needed for its execution."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0004",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Security best practices require containers to run with minimal required capabilities."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0004\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any\nMessage: Container 'app' of 'deployment' 'app' in 'default' namespace should set securityContext.capabilities.drop\nLink: [KSV-0004](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004)\nSecurity best practices require containers to run with minimal required capabilities.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0004**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any|Container 'app' of 'deployment' 'app' in 'default' namespace should set securityContext.capabilities.drop|[KSV-0004](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004)|\n\nSecurity best practices require containers to run with minimal required capabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0011",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CPU not limited"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Enforcing CPU limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0011",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0011\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: CPU not limited\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.limits.cpu'\nLink: [KSV-0011](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0011)\nEnforcing CPU limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0011**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|CPU not limited|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.limits.cpu'|[KSV-0011](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0011)|\n\nEnforcing CPU limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0012",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Runs as root user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Force the running image to run as a non-root user to ensure least privileges."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0012\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: Runs as root user\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.runAsNonRoot' to true\nLink: [KSV-0012](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012)\nForce the running image to run as a non-root user to ensure least privileges.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0012**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|MEDIUM|Runs as root user|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.runAsNonRoot' to true|[KSV-0012](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012)|\n\nForce the running image to run as a non-root user to ensure least privileges."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0013",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Image tag \":latest\" used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "It is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0013\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nCheck: Image tag \":latest\" used\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should specify an image tag\nLink: [KSV-0013](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013)\nIt is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0013**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|MEDIUM|Image tag \":latest\" used|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should specify an image tag|[KSV-0013](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013)|\n\nIt is best to avoid using the ':latest' image tag when deploying containers in production. Doing so makes it hard to track which version of the image is running, and hard to roll back the version."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0014",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Root file system is not read-only"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An immutable root file system prevents applications from writing to their local disk. This can limit intrusions, as attackers will not be able to tamper with the file system or write foreign executables to disk."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0014\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Root file system is not read-only\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.readOnlyRootFilesystem' to true\nLink: [KSV-0014](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014)\nAn immutable root file system prevents applications from writing to their local disk. This can limit intrusions, as attackers will not be able to tamper with the file system or write foreign executables to disk.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0014**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|HIGH|Root file system is not read-only|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.readOnlyRootFilesystem' to true|[KSV-0014](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014)|\n\nAn immutable root file system prevents applications from writing to their local disk. This can limit intrusions, as attackers will not be able to tamper with the file system or write foreign executables to disk."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0015",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CPU requests not specified"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When containers have resource requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0015",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0015\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: CPU requests not specified\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.requests.cpu'\nLink: [KSV-0015](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0015)\nWhen containers have resource requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0015**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|CPU requests not specified|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.requests.cpu'|[KSV-0015](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0015)|\n\nWhen containers have resource requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0016",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Memory requests not specified"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When containers have memory requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0016",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0016\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Memory requests not specified\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.requests.memory'\nLink: [KSV-0016](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0016)\nWhen containers have memory requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0016**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Memory requests not specified|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.requests.memory'|[KSV-0016](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0016)|\n\nWhen containers have memory requests specified, the scheduler can make better decisions about which nodes to place pods on, and how to deal with resource contention."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0018",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Memory not limited"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Enforcing memory limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0018",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0018\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Memory not limited\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.limits.memory'\nLink: [KSV-0018](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0018)\nEnforcing memory limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0018**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Memory not limited|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'resources.limits.memory'|[KSV-0018](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0018)|\n\nEnforcing memory limits prevents DoS via resource exhaustion."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0020",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Runs with UID \u003c= 10000"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Force the container to run with user ID \u003e 10000 to avoid conflicts with the host’s user table."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0020",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0020\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Runs with UID \u003c= 10000\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.runAsUser' \u003e 10000\nLink: [KSV-0020](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0020)\nForce the container to run with user ID \u003e 10000 to avoid conflicts with the host’s user table.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration KSV-0020**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Kubernetes Security Check|LOW|Runs with UID \u003c= 10000|Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.runAsUser' \u003e 10000|[KSV-0020](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0020)|\n\nForce the container to run with user ID \u003e 10000 to avoid conflicts with the host’s user table."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "KSV-0021",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Runs with GID \u003c= 10000"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Force the container to run with group ID \u003e 10000 to avoid conflicts with the host’s user table."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0021",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration KSV-0021\nType: Kubernetes Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: Runs with GID \u003c= 10000\nMessage: Container 'app' of Deployment 'app' should set 'securityContext.runAsGroup' \u003e 10000\nLink: [KSV-0021](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0021)\nForce the container to run with group ID \u003e 10000 to avoid conflicts with the host’s user table.",
